{"uid":"18a538df6cd0add1","name":"test_resilient_callable_timeout_returns_control_without_joining_the_orphan","fullName":"tests.test_workflow_runtime#test_resilient_callable_timeout_returns_control_without_joining_the_orphan","historyId":"3d35a9265deb86b486a92e16c36288a7","time":{"start":1789830786865,"stop":1789830787067,"duration":202},"description":"The timeout must bound the *wall clock*, not just the error message.\n\n    The pool was entered with ``with``, whose ``__exit__`` calls\n    ``shutdown(wait=True)`` and joins the thread the timeout just abandoned. So a\n    tool declaring a 0.2s timeout and sleeping 3s raised \"timed out after 0.2s\"\n    at t=3.0 — the deadline appeared in the exception and nowhere in reality,\n    which is exactly what makes a cancellation or SLO claim untrue.\n\n    The existing timeout test above uses a 10ms body, too short to tell a\n    blocking shutdown from a non-blocking one; this one is deliberately far\n    apart so the assertion cannot pass by accident.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>The timeout must bound the <em>wall clock</em>, not just the error message.</p>\n<pre><code>The pool was entered with ``with``, whose ``__exit__`` calls\n``shutdown(wait=True)`` and joins the thread the timeout just abandoned. So a\ntool declaring a 0.2s timeout and sleeping 3s raised &quot;timed out after 0.2s&quot;\nat t=3.0 — the deadline appeared in the exception and nowhere in reality,\nwhich is exactly what makes a cancellation or SLO claim untrue.\n\nThe existing timeout test above uses a 10ms body, too short to tell a\nblocking shutdown from a non-blocking one; this one is deliberately far\napart so the assertion cannot pass by accident.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1789829381910,"stop":1789829381911,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],